    "['sysname [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [0, 0], 'trans_command': 'hostname [parameter1]', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'hostname [parameter1]'}]]": 1,
    "['service-security global-binding [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip access-list extended test_global', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip access-list extended test_global', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nip access-list extended test_global\\n##  \\n\\n**Note:**  \\n1. Cisco does not have a direct 1:1 equivalent to Huawei\\'s `service-security global-binding` command, as the concept differs between vendors.  \\n2. The closest approximation is creating a globally applied ACL (access control list) in Cisco, which would need to be manually applied to interfaces as required.  \\n3. The name `test_global` is used here to indicate the global scope (Cisco ACLs are not inherently \"global-binding\" but can be applied to multiple interfaces).  \\n\\nFor complete functionality, you would also need to translate the `service-security policy` rules into Cisco ACEs (Access Control Entries) within the ACL. Example:  \\n```\\nip access-list extended test_global  \\n deny ip host 10.10.1.1 any  \\n permit ip any any  \\n```  \\nThen apply it to interfaces via:  \\n```\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0  \\n ip access-group test_global in  \\n```', 'trans_template': 'ip access-list extended test_global'}]]": 1,
    "['service-security policy [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip access-list extended test', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip access-list extended test', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here is the translated Cisco equivalent for the Huawei `service-security policy ipv4 test` command:\\n\\n##\\nip access-list extended test\\n##\\n\\nThe Huawei `service-security policy` creates a security policy (similar to an ACL in Cisco). In Cisco, the equivalent would be an extended named ACL (`ip access-list extended`). The name `test` is preserved, and the subsequent rules (like `rule 10 deny protocol ip source-ip 10.10.1.1 0`) would be translated as ACEs (Access Control Entries) under this ACL.', 'trans_template': 'ip access-list extended test'}]]": 1,
